= Sequence annotation — Simple =

Sequence annotation adds information to a DNA, RNA, or protein sequence—for example where a gene is, what a protein domain might do, or what evidence supports a feature. A prediction is not the same as experimental confirmation.

'''Important boundary:''' annotation ≠ sequence.

